    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9697" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Compsa</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of the Hirpini
				in Samnium</i>, now <i>Conza</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 23, 1,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 2, 63, 3</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Compsānus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cons-</span></b> ), a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to Compsa</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					24, 44, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Trebius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					23, 1, 1</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 61</span></i>,
			§§ 160 and 164.—In
			plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Compsāni</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cons-</span></b> ), ōrum,
			m., <i>the inhabitants of Compsa</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 11,
				16, § 105</span></i>.</div>
